INT. UNDERGROUND PARKING STRUCTURE, LEVEL P4 - NIGHT

Concrete columns. Dripping pipes. Fluorescent tubes that buzz and flicker. Oil stains like ink blots. At the far end, a stairwell door hangs ajar.

DETECTIVE IGNACIO PALAZZO-MENSAH (40s, trench coat, a limp, a gun held low) slips between two parked sedans. Behind him, FBI analyst COLLETTE ARMSTRONG-DUBOIS (30s, ballistic vest over a cardigan) clutches a laptop. In the shadows, a figure in a gray hoodie crouches: the INFORMANT, BRIDGET QUILLFEATHER (20s, nervous eyes, pale as paper). A ways off, DETECTIVE MARCUS OYELARAN-STROUD (50s, radio at his collar) circles the perimeter, and in a car at the exit ramp, driver SOPHRONIA HALLIWELL (30s, headset, steady) watches the mirror.

IGNACIO
(whispering)
Bridget, where's the package?

BRIDGET
Level three. In the van.

COLLETTE
Level three isn't on the schematic.

BRIDGET
It's not on anything.

MARCUS
(into radio)
All units, hold positions.

A steel door clangs somewhere. Everyone freezes. A distant engine idles. Headlights sweep across the pillars and swing away.

IGNACIO
(quietly, to himself)
Easy.

Collette types something silent. Bridget wipes her sweaty palms on her knees.

SOPHRONIA
(into headset)
Exit ramp clear. For now.

BRIDGET
They'll see the lights.

IGNACIO
They already know we're here.

BRIDGET
Then why--

A gunshot cracks across the garage. A windshield bursts. Ignacio shoves Bridget flat. Collette dives behind a column, laptop sliding across the concrete. Marcus sprints toward the sound. Sophronia guns the engine and the car leaps forward.

Another shot. Another. The echoes pile on each other until the whole structure rings like a struck bell.

MARCUS
(shouting)
Contact! North ramp!

IGNACIO
(to Collette)
Get her out!

COLLETTE
What about you?

IGNACIO
Go!

Collette grabs Bridget's hand and they run for the stairwell, ducking low between sedans. Ignacio rises, fires twice, and ducks.

SOPHRONIA
(over radio)
Marcus, Ignacio, I'm coming around.

Her car shrieks around a column and slams to a stop in front of Collette and Bridget. The back door flies open.

SOPHRONIA (CONT'D)
(through the window)
Get in!

They pile into the back seat. Ignacio sprints, vaults the hood, and drops into the front. Marcus dives in last. The car lurches forward as bullets rake the trunk.

MARCUS
Drive!

SOPHRONIA
I am driving!

The car roars up the ramp and out into the rain.
